project-handlers-judge.instruction:
Write ONLY the test file `api/handlers_examples_test.go`: one `func TestProjectHandlersExample<n>(t *testing.T)` per example of `api/handlers.go` taken from go.mod, in example order. Do not write or modify `api/handlers.go` or any other file: the author of the criterion is not the author of the code. The test file is in package api; it imports the standard library, the module's `morphstudio/internal/testhelp`, `morphstudio/project` and `morphstudio/store` only, and compares with `testhelp.Equal`. Never a listener: the harness is

```go
func serve(h func(http.ResponseWriter, *http.Request), method, target, id, contentType, body string) *httptest.ResponseRecorder {
	req := httptest.NewRequest(method, target, strings.NewReader(body))
	if contentType != "" {
		req.Header.Set("Content-Type", contentType)
	}
	if id != "" {
		req.SetPathValue("id", id)
	}
	rec := httptest.NewRecorder()
	h(rec, req)
	return rec
}
```

called as serve(h.Create, "POST", "/v1/projects", "", "application/json", `{...}`); compare rec.Code, rec.Header().Get("Content-Type"), rec.Body.String() (bodies end with "\n"). A failing store is a type of the test file implementing store.Store whose every method returns errors.New("disk full"). Go 1.22, gofmt-formatted.
